SUSPECTED BUG (low confidence): the wrap of a nil error is not an entry.
Retry loop with a single retryable kind: Is(ErrTimeout) -> continue, else fail fast with "job %s: %w".
As expected ErrTimeout appears ONLY with the "retries exhausted" chain and ErrNotFound, ErrRateLimited and
*NetError ONLY with "job %s: %w". But when the loop body never runs (Max == 0) the function returns
fmt.Errorf("...: %w", nil), a non-nil error with no wrapped origin; expected an extra opaque fmt.Errorf
entry for it, actual: none.
